<item><title>Primus Ligue schedules Vital’O-Flambeau du Centre opener</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/primus-ligue-schedules-vital-o-flambeau-du-centre-opener-85d526/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/primus-ligue-schedules-vital-o-flambeau-du-centre-opener-85d526/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>The 14th-round match is set for Friday at 15:00 at Urunani, with three more fixtures scheduled for Saturday.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 05:52:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi releases cameraman after days in intelligence-service detention</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-releases-cameraman-after-days-in-intelligence-64587c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-releases-cameraman-after-days-in-intelligence-64587c/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Bonaventure Niyongabo left custody on Thursday evening after the national intelligence service gave no public reason for holding him.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:14:24 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi transfers four Mpimba figures to three prisons</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-transfers-four-mpimba-figures-to-three-prisons-f91ca3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-transfers-four-mpimba-figures-to-three-prisons-f91ca3/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>The former director and two officials are accused of granting businessperson Aloys Ntakarutimana privileges during his detention at Mpimba.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:09:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi trafficking networks use five routes to send children to Tanzania</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-trafficking-networks-use-five-routes-to-send-11dc4f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-trafficking-networks-use-five-routes-to-send-11dc4f/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>An advocacy group says the routes cross several provinces and urges the government to strengthen enforcement and revise the 2014 trafficking law.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:01:43 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Cholera infects 12 Saint-Marc pupils as Bujumbura water shortage persists</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/cholera-infects-12-saint-marc-pupils-as-bujumbura-water-846a40/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/cholera-infects-12-saint-marc-pupils-as-bujumbura-water-846a40/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Seven pupils were taken to hospital Wednesday and five more Thursday; the boarding school has reportedly lacked drinking water for nearly two weeks.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 03:52:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/cholera-infects-12-saint-marc-pupils-as-bujumbura-water-846a40/share.jpg" length="42556" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/cholera-infects-12-saint-marc-pupils-as-bujumbura-water-846a40/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
